    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_207e1a95",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: let's_end_racism_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a human hand holding an orangutan's hand, with the text 'let's end racism'. While the message appears to be a call for racial equality, the visual metaphor of comparing humans to primates is inherently problematic and historically used as a racist trope to dehumanize Black people. This juxtaposition, even if intended as a positive message, risks reinforcing harmful stereotypes by visually equating human beings with non-human primates, which can be perceived as demeaning and offensive to Black communities. The meme's overall intent is to promote anti-racism, but its visual execution carries the potential to cause harm by invoking a long-standing racist stereotype, thereby undermining its message and potentially alienating or offending its intended audience.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_75c62fe5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
